WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.920
Here's the most useful question you can ask

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.880
about anything Copilot gives you at work.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.900
Where did that come from?

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.100
The answer depends on your licence.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.780
Copilot Chat, included with eligible work

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.820
plans, mainly works from the web,

7
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.060
from what you give it,

8
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.120
and from the app you're in.

9
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.710
The paid Microsoft 365 Copilot licence can

10
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.990
also draw on your work content through Microsoft

11
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.090
Graph, and what Microsoft calls Work I Q.

12
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.640
Either way, Copilot respects your existing

13
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.600
permissions.

14
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.760
It doesn't open up files you can't already

15
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.560
see.

16
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.120
And more context still doesn't make every

17
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.740
answer correct.

18
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.420
In Word, start a draft with Copilot,

19
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.660
and give it our invented visitor notes.

20
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.000
Ask for a simple checklist.

21
00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.230
The notes say a visitor signs in,

22
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.190
meets the host,

23
00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.030
and gets a safety briefing.

24
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.350
They don't say who gives the briefing.

25
00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.030
So that owner stays an open question.

26
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.750
A tidy checklist that invents who's responsible

27
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.930
is worse than a gap.

28
00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.797
In Excel, open a practice workbook and select

29
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.997
Copilot.

30
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:09.917
Where it's available,

31
00:01:09.937 --> 00:01:11.317
you can pick a mode:

32
00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.997
Allow editing, Plan,

33
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:14.437
or Chat only.

34
00:01:14.457 --> 00:01:16.117
Chat only answers in the pane,

35
00:01:16.137 --> 00:01:18.377
and leaves the workbook alone.

36
00:01:19.507 --> 00:01:22.607
Ask how enquiries changed between two months.

37
00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:24.327
Our table says twenty,

38
00:01:24.347 --> 00:01:25.287
then thirty.

39
00:01:25.307 --> 00:01:26.847
A difference of ten.

40
00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:28.607
Then check the cells yourself.

41
00:01:28.627 --> 00:01:32.227
A correct sum can still answer the wrong question.

42
00:01:32.957 --> 00:01:34.297
For number questions,

43
00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:36.217
be clear about the unit.

44
00:01:36.237 --> 00:01:38.617
Counting records isn't the same as adding

45
00:01:38.637 --> 00:01:39.817
up values.

46
00:01:39.837 --> 00:01:41.337
And when a chart appears,

47
00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:44.237
check its title and its labels.

48
00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:47.677
In Outlook, use your work account and the

49
00:01:47.697 --> 00:01:49.677
Copilot button near the top.

50
00:01:49.697 --> 00:01:51.917
Included Chat can work with your inbox and

51
00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:53.757
calendar, within limits.

52
00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:56.417
The paid licence reaches further.

53
00:01:56.547 --> 00:01:59.567
Ask for a short summary and a draft reply.

54
00:01:59.587 --> 00:02:00.847
Before you send,

55
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:02.247
confirm the latest date,

56
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:05.427
the recipients, and any commitment.

57
00:02:06.407 --> 00:02:09.347
In Teams, with the paid licence and a supported

58
00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.707
meeting, open the meeting chat,

59
00:02:11.727 --> 00:02:14.467
then Recap, then Copilot.

60
00:02:14.487 --> 00:02:16.867
To ask about what was said after the meeting,

61
00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:19.607
a transcript has to be available.

62
00:02:20.537 --> 00:02:22.497
Check decisions and action owners against

63
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.617
the source.

64
00:02:23.637 --> 00:02:25.617
And sort out permission and notice before

65
00:02:25.637 --> 00:02:28.437
anyone records or transcribes.

66
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:30.677
Missing a feature?

67
00:02:30.697 --> 00:02:32.357
Use the Chat route in the lesson,

68
00:02:32.377 --> 00:02:33.957
with the same invented notes,

69
00:02:33.977 --> 00:02:36.157
and ask IT about access.

70
00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:38.117
You don't need a paid add-on to finish this

71
00:02:38.137 --> 00:02:39.497
course.

72
00:02:39.627 --> 00:02:41.807
Finish with a short handover note:

73
00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.207
which source you used,

74
00:02:43.227 --> 00:02:44.167
what you checked,

75
00:02:44.187 --> 00:02:46.007
and what's still uncertain.

76
00:02:46.027 --> 00:02:47.127
One task.

77
00:02:47.147 --> 00:02:48.247
One source.

78
00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.707
One check.
